---

This repository bundles or builds on several open-source projects. JePT's own
code (everything outside `labelCloud/`) is MIT. The bundled `labelCloud/`
subdirectory is a modified derivative work of an upstream GPL-v3 project and
**remains under GPL v3** (see `labelCloud/LICENSE`). Distributing the
combined repository as a whole therefore requires complying with the GPL
terms for the `labelCloud/` subtree. Full attributions follow:

* LitePT — paper: Yue, Robert, Wang, Hong, Wegner, Rupprecht, Schindler
  (ETH Zurich / Oxford / UZH). "LitePT: Lighter Yet Stronger Point Transformer",
  arXiv:2512.13689, CVPR 2026. Code MIT, © Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing
  Lab (github.com/prs-eth/LitePT). Reused verbatim in `models/litept/`.

* pyLitePT — MIT, © Photogrammetry and Remote Sensing Lab. Reused in
  `pcdet_lite/`, `models/detection.py`, `models/modules.py`, `backend_cpu/`,
  `libs/`, `metrics/`, `utils/`, `hybrid_backend.py`, and adapted in
  `models/unified.py`, `data/labeled_dataset.py`.

* Point-JEPA — paper: Ayumu Saito, Prachi Kudeshia, Jiju Poovvancheri.
  "Point-JEPA: A Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture for Self-Supervised
  Learning on Point Cloud", arXiv:2404.16432. Reference-implementation code
  MIT, © 2023 Karim Abou Zeid. `jepa/ema.py` adapted from that implementation.

* labelCloud — original work © 2020-2023 Christoph Sager
  (github.com/ch-sa/labelCloud), GPL v3. Bundled under `labelCloud/` with
  modifications by Md-aliy7 (JePT data-format integration). The bundled
  `labelCloud/` subtree remains under GPL v3 — see `labelCloud/LICENSE`.
